ces must not be conflated. All chemistry excludes molecular oxygen. Surface reactions occur in shaded pores or beneath sediment skins despite strong external UV. Formulae use neutral-component bookkeeping; actual protonation depends on pH. The target node specifies connectivity without stereochemistry: formation of that connectivity does not establish the threonine/allo-threonine ratio, recoverable threonine yield, or L-enrichment. Hub annotations emphasize organic branching and convergence rather than ubiquitous water and hydrogen.\n\nMOLECULES (32 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2O (Water) [starting]\n  - mol_002: H2 (Hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_003: H3N (Ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CHN (Hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_005: CH2O (Formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_006: C2H4O (Acetaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_007: C2H2O3 (Glyoxylic acid) [starting]\n  - mol_008: C2H4N2 (Aminoacetonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C2H6N2O (Glycinamide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C2H5NO2 (Glycine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C3H6O2 (3-Hydroxypropionaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C3H4O (Acrolein) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C4H6N2 (Vinylglycine aminonitrile precursor) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_014: C4H8N2O (Vinylglycinamide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C4H7NO2 (Vinylglycine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C4H8N2O (Threonine aminonitrile precursor) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C4H10N2O2 (Threoninamide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_018: C4H9NO3 (Threonine, stereochemistry unresolved) [target]\n  - mol_019: CH4O (Methanol) [starting]\n  - mol_020: CH4S (Methyl mercaptan) [starting]\n  - mol_021: CO (Carbon monoxide) [starting]\n  - mol_022: H2S (Hydrogen sulfide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_023: C3H6OS (Methyl thioacetate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_024: C5H8O2S (S-Methyl acetoacetate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_025: C5H8O3 (Methyl acetoacetate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_026: HNO2 (Nitrous acid) [starting]\n  - mol_027: C5H7NO4 (Methyl isonitrosoacetoacetate)