ration at the aminonitrile stage. Acidic aqueous conditions can also hydrate or hydrolyze the nitrile and affect aminonitrile stability, so the stipulated transformation order is not established. Competing nitrile hydration could redirect material into another graph branch, but those branches still contain unresolved alkene-hydration steps. Atom balance alone does not establish this chemoselectivity.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_012\",\n        \"rxn_017\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Measure alkene hydration, nitrile hydration, and decomposition concurrently for the unsaturated aminonitrile.\",\n        \"Identify whether a realistic catalyst can accelerate productive alkene hydration without destructive side chemistry.\",\n        \"If reactions occur concurrently, represent and validate the resulting reaction network rather than assuming a controlled order.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_018\": 0.74,\n        \"rxn_019\": 0.25,\n        \"rxn_020\": 0.61,\n        \"rxn_021\": 0.86,\n        \"rxn_022\": 0.33,\n        \"rxn_023\": 0.62,\n        \"rxn_026\": 0.88\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.45,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.59,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.38,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.2,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.35,\n      \"feedback\": \"Metal-sulfide-associated carbonylation has relevant model-system precedent, and activated-methylene nitrosation and final ester hydrolysis are chemically credible. The major upstream bottleneck is rxn_019: productive thioester Claisen condensation requires suitable enolate generation and competition against hydrolysis. Methanolysis also requires a justified methanol activity and catalyst regime. Ketone-first hydrogenation of an oxime-bearing substrate is catalyst-dependent and cannot be assumed for an unspecified geological interface. The ackn