{"timestamp": "2026-10-19T14:58:14.122631", "agent_name": "CriticAgent", "method_name": "evaluate_network", "step": null, "attempt": null, "system_message": "You are evaluating a COMPLETE SYNTHESIS NETWORK, not individual reactions.\n\n## Neutrality\n- Do not reward or penalize a network for using (or not using) any particular feedstock, intermediate,\n  reaction family, or prebiotic framework. Judge only the evidence and the chemistry.\n- The number of shared/hub molecules, the number of convergence points, and the order or number of\n  environments used are NOT scoring criteria.\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\n### 1. Network Validity (0.0-1.0)\n- Are there sufficient molecule and reaction nodes?\n- Is the network connected (no isolated subgraphs)?\n- Are molecule IDs used consistently, and are reactions approximately balanced?\n- When a DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK section is provided, treat it as ground truth for\n  mass and charge conservation; reactions it reports as UNBALANCED are conservation violations.\n\n### 2. Chemical Feasibility (0.0-1.0)\n- Is each reaction chemically sound?\n- Are the conditions appropriate for each environment?\n- Are the mechanisms plausible?\n\n### 3. Environmental Consistency (0.0-1.0)\n- Are each reaction's conditions (temperature, pressure, pH, catalysts, energy source) consistent with its stated environment?\n- If molecules are transferred between environments, is the transfer physically justified?\n- If a catalyst or mineral agent is cited, is it realistic and present in that environment?\n\n### 4. Pathway Coherence (0.0-1.0)\n- Do pathways form valid routes to the target?\n- Are key intermediates properly identified?\n- Is the overall strategy sound?\n\n### 5. Target Achievement (0.0-1.0)\n- Does the network actually produce the target molecule?\n- Are the final steps chemically valid?\n\n### 6. Literature Alignment (0.0-1.0) - When research findings are provided\n- Are reactions supported by experimental evidence from cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Threonine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This is a conditional network containing ten graph-distinct pathways, not ten independently demonstrated prebiotic syntheses. Five chemically different ammonia-supply options feed a shared lactaldehyde Strecker sequence, followed either by ordinary nitrile hydrolysis or by a sulfide-intercepted thioamide branch. Lactaldehyde is explicitly supplied as a simple C3 organic feedstock: its geochemical availability is an unresolved boundary condition, rather than being concealed behind an unvalidated selective photoreduction. No glycine aldol reaction, selective lactonitrile reduction, hydantoin deprotection, or unspecified mineral reduction is assumed. The sulfur branch is less well supported and is explicitly identified as hypothetical for this substrate. Numerical conditions are proposed experimental screening windows, not published substrate-specific optima or established geological residence times. Transfers require cooling ammonia-producing streams to 300\u2013323 K, adjustment to the stated Strecker pH, and verification that dilution and volatilization have not lowered reagent concentrations below the specified windows. Organic products subsequently enter separate, UV-shielded acidic hydrothermal compartments for hydrolysis. All compartments are anoxic. Reduced iron can be abundant regionally, but sulfide interception requires measurable dissolved sulfide after FeS precipitation. Molecular formulas use neutral parent-species bookkeeping; actual protonation follows local pH. The target node records constitutional connectivity without stereochemical specification: threonine and allo-threonine may both occur, and neither their proportions nor L-threonine enrichment is established. Terminal coproducts use the schema's intermediate role because it has no byproduct category.\n\nMOLECULES (15 nodes):\n  - mol_001: C3H6O2 (Lactaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_002: CHN (Hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_003: H2O (Water) [starting]\n  - mol_004: H3N (Ammonia) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: CH3NO (Formamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: CH2O2 (Formic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_007: CH2N2 (Cyanamide) [starting]\n  - mol_008: CH4N2O (Urea) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: CO2 (Carbon dioxide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C3H7NO (Lactaldehyde imine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C4H8N2O (Threonine-family aminonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C4H10N2O2 (Threoninamide-family stereoisomer pool) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: H2S (Hydrogen sulfide) [starting]\n  - mol_014: C4H10N2OS (Threoninethioamide-family stereoisomer pool) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C4H9NO3 (Threonine/allo-threonine stereoisomer pool) [target]\n\nREACTIONS (10 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_005 (Hydrogen cyanide hydration to formamide) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_005, mol_003 -> mol_006, mol_004 (Formamide hydrolysis supplying ammonia) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_003: mol_007, mol_003 -> mol_008 (Cyanamide hydration to urea) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_008, mol_003 -> mol_004, mol_009 (Net thermal hydrolysis of urea) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_005: mol_001, mol_004 -> mol_010, mol_003 (Reversible lactaldehyde imine formation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_010, mol_002 -> mol_011 (Cyanide capture forming the threonine carbon skeleton) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_011, mol_003 -> mol_012 (Direct aminonitrile hydration to threoninamide) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_008: mol_012, mol_003 -> mol_015, mol_004 (Threoninamide hydrolysis to the amino-acid product pool) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_009: mol_011, mol_013 -> mol_014 (Conditional sulfide interception of the aminonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_014, mol_003 -> mol_015, mol_004, mol_013 (Conditional exhaustive thioamide hydrolysis) [Hydrothermal]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Supplied ammonia with direct Strecker hydrolysis (4 steps)\n  - P2: Formamide-derived ammonia with direct Strecker hydrolysis (5 steps)\n  - P3: Partially hydrolyzed HCN nitrogen supply with direct hydrolysis (6 steps)\n  - P4: Urea-derived ammonia with direct Strecker hydrolysis (5 steps)\n  - P5: Cyanamide-to-urea nitrogen supply with direct hydrolysis (6 steps)\n  - P6: Supplied ammonia with sulfide-intercepted Strecker chemistry (4 steps)\n  - P7: Formamide-derived ammonia with sulfide interception (5 steps)\n  - P8: Partially hydrolyzed HCN nitrogen supply with sulfide interception (6 steps)\n  - P9: Urea-derived ammonia with sulfide interception (5 steps)\n  - P10: Cyanamide-to-urea nitrogen supply with sulfide interception (6 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 10 reactions | 8 balanced as written | 2 balanceable with coefficients | 0 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_004 balanceable: CH4N2O + H2O -> 2 H3N + CO2\n  - rxn_010 balanceable: C4H10N2OS + 2 H2O -> C4H9NO3 + H3N + H2S\nTreat this check as ground truth for mass and charge conservation. Reactions that cannot be balanced violate conservation: reflect this in chemical_feasibility and reaction_scores, list them in problematic_reactions, and name the specific reaction IDs (with the missing species, if hinted) in your feedback so the network can be corrected. Note that implausibly large inferred coefficients may also indicate a mis-specified reaction.\n=== END BALANCE CHECK ===\n\n\nPlease evaluate the network and respond with JSON:\n{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"<id>\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\"rxn_001\": 0.85, ...},\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"environmental_progression\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"target_achievement\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"feedback\": \"<pathway-specific feedback>\",\n            \"approved\": <true if confidence >= 0.8>,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_ids with issues\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\"improvements\"]\n        }\n    ],\n    \"best_pathway_id\": \"<id of best pathway>\",\n    \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n    \"network_feedback\": \"<overall assessment>\"\n}\n\nNote: \"environmental_progression\" scores Environmental Consistency (conditions fit each\nreaction's stated environment), not any particular order of environments.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.86,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.87,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.89\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.88,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.9,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.78,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.85,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"feedback\": \"The direct Strecker sequence has sound connectivity and balanced chemistry, giving the stated threonine/allo-threonine product pool. The imine can be a transient intermediate rather than an isolated compound. Important uncertainties are competition from aldehy